<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert II, Count of Artois</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1250–1302</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert II was count of Artois from his birth in 1250, the son of Robert I, who had been killed at al-Mansurah. A leading French commander, he served in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> for his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a>, defeated the Flemings at Furnes in 1297 and led the French army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kortrijk">Courtrai</a> in 1302, where he was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-golden-spurs">Battle of the Golden Spurs</a>. His daughter Mahaut inherited the county.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-ii-count-of-artois.jpg" alt="Robert II, Count of Artois" width="208" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis DESCHAMPS DE PAS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert2Artois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
